<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.1.1: Understanding Value</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00051</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.1.1: Understanding Value</md:title>
    <md:uuid>5da5f37b-8f5f-4fce-a198-8c20e6b94cbc</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<para>Here are some letters and what they represent. All costs are in dollars.</para>
<list>
  <list>
    <item>\( m \) represents the cost of a main dish.</item>
    <item>\( n \) represents the number of side dishes.</item>
    <item>\( s \) represents the cost of a side dish.</item>
    <item>\( t \) represents the total cost of a meal.</item>
  </list>
</list>
<para>For questions 1 - 4, discuss what each <term data-schema-version="1.0" data-store="glossary-tooltip">equation</term> means with a partner. Then, describe the situation in words.

</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>\( m=7.50 \)</item>
</list>
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </problem><solution>
    
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>A main dish costs $7.50.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>\( m = s + 4.50 \)</item>
</list>
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </problem><solution>
    
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Your answer may vary, but here are some examples. </para>
    <list>
      <item>The cost of a main dish is the cost of the side dish plus $4.50.</item>
      <item>
        The cost of a main dish is $4.50 more than the cost of a side dish.
      </item>
    </list>
  </solution></exercise>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>\( ns = 6 \)</item>
</list>
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </problem><solution>
    
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>The number of side dishes times the cost of the side dish is \($6\).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>\( m + ns = t \)</item>
</list>
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </problem><solution>
    
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>The main dish added to the quantity of the number of side dishes times the cost of the side dish represents the total cost of the meal.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item>Write a new equation that could be true in this same situation. </item>
</list>
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </problem><solution>
    
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Your answer may vary, but here are some examples.</para>
    <list>
      <item>\(m = 2\)</item>
      <item> \(m - s = 4.5\)</item>
      <item> \(m + 6 = 13.5\)</item>
    </list>
  </solution></exercise>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item>Describe what your new equation means in words. </item>
</list>
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </problem><solution>
    
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Your answer may vary, but here are some examples. </para>
    <list>
      <item>The main dish costs \($2\).</item>
      <item> The difference in cost between the main dish and a side dish is \($4.50\).</item>
      <item> \($13.50\) is the cost of the main dish and a \($6\) tip.
      </item>
    </list>
  </solution></exercise></section>
